                <pb facs="0281" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-01-26T17:00:00-03:00">January 26, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 26—4:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>41. Department’s 19, January 25, 7 p.m. Aranha is in Uruguay. I discussed the
                    matter with Nabuco and he says that he agrees with the Department’s point of
                    view and will instruct the Brazilian chiefs of mission along the lines indicated
                    by the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
